meta {
  name: saveAttachment
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: https://{{customer}}.{{domain}}/jsonrpc
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "method": "saveAttachment",
    "params": {
      "product_attachment_type_code": "MAN",
      "source_type": "URL",
      "source_url": "https://example.com/manual.pdf",
      "language": "en"
    },
    "id": 1
  }
}

docs {
  Create or update a document attachment

  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `product_attachment_id` | integer (nullable) | no | Internal ID of the attachment; omit to create a new attachment |
  | `product_attachment_type_code` | string (nullable) | no | Type code classifying the attachment (e.g. TECHNICAL, SAFETY) |
  | `language` | string (nullable) | no | Language code for the attachment; null for language-neutral attachments |
  | `source_type` | string (nullable) | no | Whether the attachment is an uploaded file (FILE) or a URL reference (URL) |
  | `source_url` | string (nullable) | no | URL of the attachment when source_type is URL |
  | `for_internal_use` | boolean (nullable) | no | True if this attachment is for internal use only and should not be published |
  | `certificate_number` | string (nullable) | no | Certificate or approval number |
  | `certificate_issuer` | string (nullable) | no | Organisation that issued the certificate |
  | `certificate_issue_date` | string (nullable) | no | Date the certificate was issued (ISO 8601) |
  | `certificate_revision_date` | string (nullable) | no | Date of the most recent certificate revision (ISO 8601) |
  | `certificate_expiration_date` | string (nullable) | no | Date the certificate expires (ISO 8601) |
  | `certificate_claim_code` | string (nullable) | no | Standardised claim code associated with the certificate |
  | `attachment_file_base64` | string (nullable) | no | Base64-encoded file content when source_type is FILE |
  | `file_name` | string (nullable) | no | Display name for the file; only valid for source_type FILE; can be set independently of attachment_file_base64 |
  | `_translations` | object[] (nullable) | no | Translated title and description for each language |
  | `_attributes` | object[] (nullable) | no | Arbitrary key-value attributes for this attachment |

  **Example: Create a URL attachment**. Use source_type=FILE with attachment_file_base64 to upload a file instead.

  ```json
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "method": "saveAttachment",
    "params": {
      "product_attachment_type_code": "MAN",
      "source_type": "URL",
      "source_url": "https://example.com/manual.pdf",
      "language": "en"
    },
    "id": 1
  }
  ```

  Result:

  ```json
  {
    "product_attachment_id": 1
  }
  ```

  **Example: Create attachment with translations and attributes**

  ```json
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "method": "saveAttachment",
    "params": {
      "product_attachment_type_code": "MAN",
      "source_type": "URL",
      "source_url": "https://example.com/manual.pdf",
      "_translations": [
        {
          "language": "en",
          "product_attachment_title": "Instruction manual",
          "product_attachment_description": "English instruction manual"
        },
        {
          "language": "nl",
          "product_attachment_title": "Gebruiksaanwijzing",
          "product_attachment_description": "Nederlandstalige gebruiksaanwijzing"
        }
      ],
      "_attributes": [
        {
          "attachment_attribute_name": "MANCategory",
          "attachment_attribute_value": "USE"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": 1
  }
  ```

  Result:

  ```json
  {
    "product_attachment_id": 1
  }
  ```
}
